WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.990 --> 00:22.410
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
...that upon your back

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
...towards the distant future

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Young boy, become a legend

01:31.900 --> 01:36.450
Correct, I have already arranged it
with the committee.

01:36.450 --> 01:38.950
The cargo left from Sasebo Port yesterday,

01:38.950 --> 01:40.830
and is now making its way here
across the Pacific Ocean.

01:44.410 --> 01:47.120
A MIG-55 D transport helicopter!

01:47.120 --> 01:50.790
I'd never have had the chance to fly in one
if it weren't for something like this.

01:50.790 --> 01:54.670
Man, this is what friends are for, right, Shinji?

01:55.510 --> 01:59.180
I figured you'd get claustrophobic looking at
the same mountains day after day,

01:59.180 --> 02:02.310
so I invited you on a date,
since it is a Sunday.

02:02.310 --> 02:06.430
What?! Then today is a real date?

02:06.430 --> 02:11.110
I bought this cap just for today, Miss Misato!

02:11.110 --> 02:13.020
So, where are we headed?

02:13.020 --> 02:16.030
We're taking a little jaunt across the Pacific
on a gorgeous cruise ship.

02:18.860 --> 02:23.120
Wow! Five aircraft carriers and
four battleships! What a fleet!

02:23.120 --> 02:26.080
This really IS what friends are for!

02:26.080 --> 02:28.210
That's your gorgeous cruise ship?

02:28.210 --> 02:29.540
Yeah, she sure is gorgeous!

02:29.540 --> 02:31.670
That's the pride of the U.N.,
the glorious regular carrier

02:31.670 --> 02:33.500
"Over the Rainbow"!

02:33.670 --> 02:34.920
It's huge.

02:35.000 --> 02:38.010
I'm surprised that such a relic is still afloat.

02:38.170 --> 02:39.470
Nah, it's not so bad.

02:39.470 --> 02:42.640
It's a vintage model from before
the Second lmpact.

02:43.550 --> 02:46.310
Give me a break!

02:46.310 --> 02:49.140
Here comes the socket for that kid's toy.

02:49.140 --> 02:50.230
What a child's errand!

03:00.910 --> 03:02.370
Awesome! Awesome!

03:02.370 --> 03:03.660
Awesome! Awesome!

03:03.660 --> 03:05.700
Awesome! Awesome! Awesome!

03:05.700 --> 03:06.830
This is way too awesome!

03:06.830 --> 03:10.040
Real men shed tears for this kind of thing!

03:10.710 --> 03:14.790
Awesome! Awesome! Awesome!
Awesome! Awesome!

03:14.790 --> 03:17.130
Hey, wait! Wait up!

03:21.720 --> 03:23.930
Damn it!

03:23.930 --> 03:25.510
Stop! Stop already!

03:29.730 --> 03:31.560
Hello, Misato.

03:31.560 --> 03:33.860
How have you been?

03:33.860 --> 03:36.650
Fine. How about you?
You've grown some, haven't you?

03:36.650 --> 03:41.200
Yeah! I'm not just taller,
my figure's filled out as well.

03:41.200 --> 03:42.570
Let me introduce you.

03:42.570 --> 03:46.950
This is the pilot of Evangelion Unit 02,
the Second Child,

03:46.950 --> 03:49.040
Asuka Langley Sohryu.

03:51.330 --> 03:53.460
Episode 8

03:51.830 --> 03:53.460
Asuka

03:52.330 --> 03:53.460
Arrives in Japan

03:53.670 --> 03:55.380
What did you do that for?!

03:57.090 --> 03:59.710
That's the viewing fee.
Quite a bargain, don't you think?

03:59.710 --> 04:03.430
What? Well then, take a look at this!

04:05.220 --> 04:06.930
What the hell are you doing?!

04:08.470 --> 04:11.930
So, which one is the famous Third Child?

04:11.930 --> 04:13.850
Don't tell me that was him.

04:13.850 --> 04:16.980
No, it's him.

04:16.980 --> 04:20.190
Well, he looks kind of dull.

04:20.190 --> 04:24.780
Well, well, I thought you were the leader
of this gang of Boy Scouts,

04:24.780 --> 04:28.200
but it seems I was mistaken.

04:28.200 --> 04:31.500
Thank you for your understanding, Captain.

04:31.500 --> 04:37.340
Oh no, thank you for giving me the
opportunity to baby-sit some kids.

04:37.340 --> 04:42.050
We appreciate your assistance
in the transport of Unit 02.

04:42.050 --> 04:44.720
Here are the specs for the
emergency power supply socket.

04:46.180 --> 04:51.390
In the first place, I haven't heard anything
about activating that toy while at sea.

04:51.390 --> 04:55.980
Why don't you just think of this as
being prepared for an emergency?

04:55.980 --> 05:01.190
That's why the Pacific Fleet is escorting it.

05:01.190 --> 05:05.280
When did the UN Navy
become a cargo service?

05:05.280 --> 05:09.450
It believe it was just after a certain
organization was established.

05:09.450 --> 05:12.540
Quite a grandiose escort for
transporting one single toy!

05:12.540 --> 05:14.870
After all, this is the entire Pacific Fleet.

05:14.870 --> 05:18.580
It's still not enough, considering
the importance of the Eva.

05:18.580 --> 05:20.380
Would you sign this document?

05:20.380 --> 05:23.710
Not yet. Eva Unit 02 and its pilot
have been entrusted to us

05:23.710 --> 05:26.680
by the Third Branch in Germany.

05:26.680 --> 05:28.890
You can't just do as you please!

05:28.890 --> 05:30.760
Then, when will you transfer them to us?

05:30.760 --> 05:33.560
Once we've unloaded in New Yokosuka.

05:33.560 --> 05:36.310
The ocean is our jurisdiction.

05:36.310 --> 05:38.230
You will follow our orders here.

05:38.230 --> 05:39.860
I understand.

05:39.860 --> 05:42.820
However, I should remind you that,
in the case of an emergency,

05:42.820 --> 05:45.610
Nerv's authority overrides yours.

05:45.610 --> 05:47.280
She's cool!

05:47.280 --> 05:48.820
She's practically like Miss Ritsuko.

05:48.820 --> 05:51.370
You're as gallant as ever.

05:51.370 --> 05:52.540
Kaji!

05:54.750 --> 05:58.000
Mr. Kaji, I don't recall inviting you
onto the bridge.

05:58.000 --> 05:59.750
Oh, sorry about that.

05:59.750 --> 06:04.840
Excuse us, then. We're counting on you to
escort us to New Yokosuka as ordered.

06:00.750 --> 06:03.090
This is a date?

06:03.090 --> 06:04.840
Awesome! Too awesome!

06:04.840 --> 06:08.550
Shit! Those kids are really going
to save the Earth?

06:08.550 --> 06:10.720
Times are changing.

06:10.720 --> 06:13.970
I understand that Congress has also
pinned its hopes on that robot.

06:13.970 --> 06:17.560
On that toy? The idiots!

06:17.560 --> 06:21.230
If they've got the money for it,
they should give it to us!

06:25.190 --> 06:28.650
What are you doing here?!

06:28.650 --> 06:30.280
Accompanying her.

06:30.280 --> 06:32.120
I'm on a business trip from Germany.

06:32.120 --> 06:36.870
Man, was I careless.
I should have anticipated this.

06:36.870 --> 06:38.750
Hey! Don't touch me!

06:38.750 --> 06:40.000
I can't help it!

06:40.000 --> 06:42.840
Squadron 3 will sortie as scheduled.

06:42.840 --> 06:45.840
Seeing anyone right now?

06:45.840 --> 06:48.220
And that would be your business WHY?

06:48.220 --> 06:51.010
What? You're kind of cold.

06:51.470 --> 06:54.180
I hear that you're living with Katsuragi?

06:54.180 --> 06:56.020
Yes.

06:56.020 --> 06:59.350
So, does she still toss and turn in bed?

07:01.940 --> 07:04.190
Wha... wha...

07:04.190 --> 07:06.070
What are you saying?!

07:06.900 --> 07:09.570
So, she hasn't changed, has she,
Mister Shinji Ikari?

07:09.570 --> 07:11.160
Well...

07:11.160 --> 07:13.620
Huh? How do you know my name?

07:13.620 --> 07:15.160
Well, of course I do.

07:15.160 --> 07:17.950
You're famous in our business.

07:17.950 --> 07:21.500
The Third Child, who piloted an Eva
in battle with no training.

07:22.420 --> 07:25.500
Oh, no, it was just luck.

07:25.500 --> 07:28.880
Luck is a part of your destiny. It's your talent.

07:29.760 --> 07:31.430
Well, I'll see you later.

07:31.430 --> 07:31.800
See you.

07:31.800 --> 07:33.720
This has got to be a bad joke.
No, a nightmare.

07:36.510 --> 07:38.810
So, what do you think about
Mister Shinji Ikari?

07:38.810 --> 07:43.650
He's boring. That's the great Third Child?
What a disappointment.

07:43.650 --> 07:48.190
Yet his sync ratio was well over 40%
in combat with no training.

07:48.190 --> 07:49.740
No way!

07:49.740 --> 07:52.610
That captain's attitude gets on my nerves.

07:52.610 --> 07:54.740
He's a proud man.

07:54.740 --> 07:57.410
Pride can make you sarcastic.

07:57.410 --> 08:00.620
That Mr. Kaji is pretty lively and funny.

08:00.620 --> 08:03.210
He hasn't changed at all, that jerk.

08:03.210 --> 08:04.380
Hey, Third Child!

08:05.790 --> 08:07.090
Come with me!

08:15.340 --> 08:18.930
So Unit 02 is red? I didn't know that.

08:18.930 --> 08:22.100
The color isn't the only difference.

08:22.100 --> 08:24.230
After all, Units 00 and 01 were created

08:24.230 --> 08:27.310
as part of a development process,
prototype and test type.

08:27.310 --> 08:32.320
The fact that it synchronized with an
untrained pilot like you is proof of that.

08:32.320 --> 08:34.780
But Unit 02 is different.

08:34.780 --> 08:36.820
Created for actual combat conditions,

08:36.820 --> 08:40.120
this is the world's first true Evangelion.

08:40.120 --> 08:41.700
This is the final model!

08:43.910 --> 08:45.420
What was that?

08:45.420 --> 08:48.090
An undersea shock wave!

08:48.090 --> 08:49.170
That explosion was nearby!

08:51.050 --> 08:51.710
What's that?

08:56.140 --> 08:57.850
Could it be an Angel?

08:57.850 --> 08:59.390
That? A real one?

09:01.470 --> 09:04.940
What'll we do? We have to get back
to Miss Misato.

09:07.060 --> 09:08.310
This is my chance!

09:13.740 --> 09:17.200
All ships take evasive action,
but watch the formation!

09:17.200 --> 09:18.780
Where's the status report?

09:18.780 --> 09:23.000
The Cymbeline's gone silent.
Titus Andronicus can't locate the target!

09:23.000 --> 09:25.710
Damn it! What in the hell is going on here?!

09:25.710 --> 09:27.710
Hello, Nerv calling.

09:27.710 --> 09:31.050
Interested in info on the unknown enemy
and the appropriate countermeasures?

09:31.050 --> 09:34.220
This is a combat situation!
No non-essential personnel allowed!

09:34.220 --> 09:37.930
This is just my opinion, but I'd say
this must be an Angel attack.

09:37.930 --> 09:40.010
All ships, fire at will!

09:40.010 --> 09:40.300
Roger.

09:40.300 --> 09:41.140
It's pointless.
Roger.

09:51.820 --> 09:55.490
So an AT field can't be penetrated
with this kind of firepower.

09:55.490 --> 09:58.450
But why is an Angel here?

09:58.450 --> 09:59.530
Could it be after Unit 02?

10:02.790 --> 10:04.660
Hey, where are we going?

10:06.830 --> 10:08.370
Just wait here a second.

10:09.580 --> 10:11.090
What's going on?

10:19.390 --> 10:21.760
Don't peep, you pervert!

10:19.840 --> 10:21.180
Sorry!

10:21.760 --> 10:24.640
Why are all boys such perverted jerks?

10:32.610 --> 10:34.360
Here we go, Asuka.

10:41.410 --> 10:42.830
Why won't it sink?!

10:42.830 --> 10:45.370
I knew it. Only an Eva can beat it!

10:50.920 --> 10:52.540
Come on, let's go.

10:53.340 --> 10:55.750
You're coming with me!

10:58.010 --> 11:01.680
Hey, why'd we change into these plug suits?

11:01.680 --> 11:03.050
What are you, stupid?

11:03.050 --> 11:06.140
What else? We're going to beat it
with my Unit 02!

11:07.680 --> 11:10.810
No way! Do you have permission
from Miss Misato?

11:10.810 --> 11:12.650
I can get permission after I've beaten it.

11:15.360 --> 11:19.650
Now, I'll show you how magnificent
my piloting is, up close and personal!

11:20.200 --> 11:22.070
Just don't disturb me.

11:27.620 --> 11:30.460
This is odd. It almost seems to be
looking for something.

11:31.620 --> 11:34.000
For an Angel to attack here...

11:34.000 --> 11:35.840
Isn't it a little different from the deal we had?

11:35.840 --> 11:37.840
This is what Unit 02 is for,

11:37.840 --> 11:40.170
and I've generously provided
a second pilot as a reserve.

11:41.050 --> 11:44.930
If worse comes to worst, escape by yourself.

11:45.680 --> 11:46.720
I know.

11:49.560 --> 11:51.850
LCL Füllung.

11:51.850 --> 11:54.060
Anfang der Bewegung.

11:54.060 --> 11:56.860
Anfang des Nervenanschlusses.

11:56.860 --> 11:59.940
Auslösung von Linkskleigung.

11:59.940 --> 12:01.570
Synchro-start.

12:05.370 --> 12:07.200
Program error? What happened?

12:07.200 --> 12:10.370
Thought noise! I told you not to disturb me.

12:10.370 --> 12:11.410
What do you mean?

12:11.410 --> 12:15.830
You're thinking in Japanese, aren't you?
Think in German.

12:15.830 --> 12:19.420
Oh, okay. Baumkuchen...

12:19.420 --> 12:25.010
Idiot! Just forget it.
Switch the base language to Japanese.

12:27.760 --> 12:30.310
Evangelion Unit 02, activate.

12:30.980 --> 12:34.020
Telex from the Othello! Unit 02 is in
the process of activation.

12:34.020 --> 12:35.060
What the...

12:35.060 --> 12:36.150
Nice going, Asuka!

12:38.980 --> 12:41.780
No! Abort the activation sequence!
Reset it!

12:42.440 --> 12:44.450
Don't worry about him, Asuka! Just launch!

12:44.450 --> 12:45.950
What are you saying?!

12:46.030 --> 12:49.950
You can't just violate my command authority
over the Eva and its pilot!

12:49.950 --> 12:51.790
What are you talking about?
This is an emergency!

12:51.790 --> 12:53.500
Who gives a damn about your procedures?

12:54.250 --> 12:56.000
Are you really serious?

12:56.000 --> 12:59.090
Unit 02 is still using type B equipment!

12:59.090 --> 13:01.550
Wouldn't it be bad if we fell in the sea?

13:01.550 --> 13:03.050
So we don't fall in.

13:03.050 --> 13:04.720
Shinji, are you in there too?

13:04.720 --> 13:05.510
Yes.

13:05.510 --> 13:07.140
Two kids!

13:07.140 --> 13:08.890
Good chance to test it...

13:08.890 --> 13:10.060
Asuka, launch!

13:12.680 --> 13:13.770
It's coming!

13:13.770 --> 13:14.350
Here we go!

13:22.110 --> 13:23.360
Where is it?

13:22.900 --> 13:23.530
That way!

13:25.150 --> 13:26.950
We've only got 58 seconds left!

13:26.950 --> 13:28.780
I know that! Misato!

13:28.780 --> 13:31.370
Get the external power supply onto the deck.

13:32.040 --> 13:33.160
Understood.

13:33.160 --> 13:34.500
What is she going to do?

13:34.500 --> 13:36.000
Okay, we're going to jump!

13:36.000 --> 13:36.710
Jump?

13:41.210 --> 13:42.550
Run!

13:54.930 --> 13:56.600
The reserve power supply is in place!

13:56.600 --> 13:58.520
Reactor connection completed!

13:58.520 --> 13:59.810
Evacuate the flight deck!

13:59.810 --> 14:01.440
The deck is ready for Eva landing!

14:01.770 --> 14:03.780
All hands, prepare for impact!

14:03.780 --> 14:04.490
I can't believe this!

14:04.490 --> 14:07.400
Eva 02, landing on deck!

14:17.160 --> 14:18.750
What a waste!

14:18.750 --> 14:21.340
Target is approaching rapidly!

14:21.340 --> 14:23.500
It's coming! Port, 9 o'clock!

14:23.500 --> 14:24.760
Switching to external power!

14:28.590 --> 14:30.010
Switch completed.

14:31.260 --> 14:32.680
But we don't have any weapons.

14:32.680 --> 14:34.140
The prog knife will be more than enough.

14:42.980 --> 14:44.360
It's pretty big.

14:44.360 --> 14:45.570
That's what I figured!

14:47.780 --> 14:49.200
What are they going to do?!

14:49.200 --> 14:51.910
Hand-to-hand combat is the best way
to defeat Angels.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.710
Good work stopping it, Asuka!

15:06.710 --> 15:09.760
That's not funny! The flight deck is a mess!

15:16.770 --> 15:18.560
Hey, they fell!

15:18.560 --> 15:19.440
Asuka!

15:19.440 --> 15:22.100
It's impossible to fight underwater
with the type-B equipment!

15:22.100 --> 15:25.320
You never know unless you try!

15:43.630 --> 15:45.630
What a waste!

15:45.630 --> 15:46.800
How much cable is left?

15:48.130 --> 15:49.880
Another 1,200 meters!

15:49.880 --> 15:51.340
What are you going to do?

15:51.340 --> 15:52.340
We'll manage somehow.

15:53.260 --> 15:54.510
I've got to do something.

15:58.680 --> 16:01.230
The cable's going to run out!
Brace for the shock!

16:07.150 --> 16:08.440
Shoot!

16:08.440 --> 16:10.150
Eva lost the target!

16:10.150 --> 16:12.320
Now's the time to change disks...

16:14.030 --> 16:15.910
A Yak 38 Custom!

16:15.910 --> 16:17.830
Hey, Katsuragi!

16:17.830 --> 16:18.910
Kaji!

16:19.660 --> 16:22.210
I've got something to deliver,
so I'll be taking off now.

16:24.290 --> 16:25.500
Launch!

16:25.880 --> 16:28.840
Take care of the rest of this,
Captain Katsuragi.

16:31.010 --> 16:32.670
He ran away.

16:32.670 --> 16:35.010
The target is approaching Eva again!

16:35.760 --> 16:36.470
It's coming again!

16:37.470 --> 16:39.310
I'll finish it off this time.

16:42.890 --> 16:45.310
What?! It's not working!

16:45.310 --> 16:46.730
That's because this is B-type equipment.

16:46.730 --> 16:48.400
What're you going to do?!

16:48.400 --> 16:49.400
What am I supposed to do?

16:49.400 --> 16:52.400
You're pretty pitiful for being the Third Child!

16:52.400 --> 16:52.900
Here it comes!

16:57.620 --> 16:59.540
A mouth?!

16:59.540 --> 17:00.830
Well, it is an Angel.

17:03.710 --> 17:06.500
Eva 02 has entered the target's body.

17:06.500 --> 17:08.420
Doesn't that mean they've been eaten?

17:10.670 --> 17:12.880
It's practically like we're fishing!

17:12.880 --> 17:15.380
Fishing? Yes, fishing!

17:17.640 --> 17:19.510
We're right back in a pinch now.

17:19.510 --> 17:20.930
Shut up!

17:21.560 --> 17:24.100
Hey, get off me already, you pervert!

17:24.100 --> 17:26.140
But we've got to free ourselves somehow.

17:26.140 --> 17:27.730
Asuka, do you read me?

17:27.730 --> 17:29.360
Don't let go, no matter what!

17:30.770 --> 17:31.860
Captain...

17:31.860 --> 17:33.030
What?

17:33.030 --> 17:34.740
I'm requesting your cooperation.

17:36.700 --> 17:40.160
A point-blank assault by two
of the surviving battleships?!

17:40.160 --> 17:41.240
Correct.

17:41.240 --> 17:46.580
We'll scuttle two of the evacuated battleships
along the umbilical cable and set a trap.

17:47.000 --> 17:50.670
During that time, Eva 02 will open
the target's mouth,

17:50.670 --> 17:52.460
both ships will rush in,

17:52.460 --> 17:55.170
fire all of their bow turret cannons,

17:55.170 --> 17:58.090
and then self-destruct, destroying the target.

17:58.260 --> 17:59.970
That's absurd!

17:59.970 --> 18:03.140
Absurd, perhaps, but I don't think
it's impossible.

18:04.180 --> 18:05.390
I understand.

18:05.390 --> 18:08.850
All hands, abandon ship!
Repeat, all hands, abandon ship!

18:08.850 --> 18:11.820
All frigates, hurry and rescue the lifeboats!

18:12.270 --> 18:14.400
But what about the Eva?

18:14.400 --> 18:17.150
Not to worry. They'll be fine.

18:17.150 --> 18:20.700
Hey! Don't use Unit 02
without my permission!

18:21.120 --> 18:23.660
Do the two of you understand the operation?

18:23.660 --> 18:25.160
I'll do my best.

18:25.160 --> 18:26.040
I'm counting on you.

18:29.790 --> 18:33.960
Both ships have opened the Kingston valve!
Scuttling towards point Z.

18:33.960 --> 18:35.010
Roger!

18:35.010 --> 18:36.090
Cable reverse!

18:43.720 --> 18:45.270
Eva has started to surface!

18:45.270 --> 18:46.810
T-minus 70 to contact!

18:48.520 --> 18:51.900
Hey, how long are you going to stay there?
Get off me already!

18:51.900 --> 18:55.150
But we've got to pry open its mouth soon,
or we'll be killed too!

18:58.780 --> 19:00.660
T-minus 60 to contact.

19:00.660 --> 19:01.950
Status on the Angel's mouth?

19:01.490 --> 19:02.450
It's still not open!

19:05.080 --> 19:08.160
Both battleships are sinking
towards the target.

19:08.160 --> 19:10.750
Eva is continuing to surface,
T-minus 50 to contact.

19:10.750 --> 19:11.630
It's not working!

19:11.630 --> 19:13.040
There's no time left!

19:19.050 --> 19:21.010
Target has passed beneath the Tempest!

19:21.010 --> 19:22.300
Speed of ascent increasing!

19:22.300 --> 19:23.720
You're not going to make it! Hurry!

19:24.140 --> 19:25.970
Don't get any strange ideas.

19:25.970 --> 19:26.850
About what?

19:26.850 --> 19:29.310
Anyway, just focus your thoughts.

19:29.310 --> 19:29.890
I know!

19:35.480 --> 19:37.280
T-minus 20 to contact!

19:39.860 --> 19:42.070
T-minus 15 to contact!

19:42.070 --> 19:44.240
Open! Open! Open! Open!

19:44.240 --> 19:46.410
Open! Open! Open! Open!

19:57.920 --> 19:58.760
Fire!

20:16.900 --> 20:20.360
New Yokosuka (Old Odawara)

20:21.570 --> 20:23.410
You certainly went all-out.

20:23.410 --> 20:26.700
I should have anticipated
underwater combat.

20:26.990 --> 20:29.370
Oh, how rare. Remorse?

20:29.370 --> 20:32.960
Who cares? We collected valuable data too.

20:32.960 --> 20:33.920
That's true.

20:34.830 --> 20:36.080
Misato...

20:36.840 --> 20:38.340
This really is something special.

20:45.340 --> 20:46.890
They MATCH!

20:46.890 --> 20:48.850
I don't believe this!

20:48.850 --> 20:51.310
They broke their synchronization
ratio records, didn't they?

20:51.310 --> 20:54.480
For only seven seconds.
It must have been due to the danger.

20:55.810 --> 20:57.480
Hey, where's Mr. Kaji?

20:57.480 --> 21:01.400
He ran off. That idiot's got to be back
at headquarters by now!

21:02.780 --> 21:06.030
It was a pretty eventful trip.

21:06.570 --> 21:08.490
Was it caused by this, after all?

21:13.210 --> 21:15.920
It's already restored itself this far.

21:15.920 --> 21:20.250
It's frozen inside dura-bakelite,
but it's still alive.

21:20.250 --> 21:24.130
Without a doubt, this is the keystone of the
Human Instrumentality Project, isn't it?

21:24.130 --> 21:25.130
Correct.

21:25.130 --> 21:27.260
This is the first human being.

21:27.260 --> 21:28.180
Adam.

21:29.300 --> 21:34.100
She may have looked cute,
but she was a real bitch.

21:34.100 --> 21:37.060
Well, we won't have to see her again.

21:37.060 --> 21:39.770
Yeah, though ol' Mister Big Shot
has to see her at work.

21:39.770 --> 21:41.400
Man, I feel sorry for ya.

21:55.000 --> 21:58.460
My name is Asuka Langley Sohryu.
Nice to meet you.

21:58.500 --> 22:00.460
TO BE CONTINUED

23:05.900 --> 23:06.820
PREVIEW

23:07.280 --> 23:09.700
Asuka and Shinji, who are on completely
different wavelengths,

23:09.700 --> 23:11.870
are soundly beaten by an Angel.

23:11.870 --> 23:15.540
Aiming for perfect unison between the two,
Misato comes up with a plan.

23:15.540 --> 23:18.660
Next episode:
"Moment and Heart Together"

23:18.660 --> 23:20.960
I'll give you more fan service next time!

23:18.830 --> 23:20.870
MOMENT AND HEART TOGETHER
